window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-c7393fbab700d02d"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"work-with-pages\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">使用页面</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取文档的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>页面是一种文档，你可以直接编辑，也可以与 ChatGPT 一起编辑。可用页面记录笔记、计划、研究内容，或保存希望日后查阅的共享参考资料。</p> <p><a id=\"create-a-focused-page\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"create-a-page\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">创建页面</h2> <p>在 Space 侧边栏中选择 <strong>New page（新建页面）</strong>，也可以请 ChatGPT 根据现有对话创建页面。选择 <strong>Pages（页面）</strong>，即可查找你创建或有权访问的页面。</p> <p>为页面命名，然后输入或粘贴内容。你可以按需添加标题、列表、图像、文件和表格。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Space 侧边栏中突出显示“新建页面”，并显示“全部”“页面”“网站”“图像”和 Google Drive 导航项。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"add-content-with-the-insert-menu\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">使用插入菜单添加内容</h2> <p>页面以区块组织内容，例如标题、段落和表格。编辑时输入 <code>/</code> 可打开插入菜单，并添加新区块。搜索要添加的内容，再选择相应选项。除了标题、列表和清单外，菜单还提供了组合辅助材料和交互式内容的方式：</p> <ul> <li><strong>表格、代码和高亮：</strong> 用于比较信息、分享代码，或突出显示备注。</li> <li><strong>图像和文件：</strong> 用于生成或上传图像，也可以附加供读者下载的文件。</li> <li><strong>页面和页面链接：</strong> 用于创建子页面，或链接到现有页面。</li> <li><strong>文件、页面和聊天：</strong> 引用已有材料，而不复制其内容。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-989576428b6123b7\"><strong>可视化</strong></a>：创建交互式计算器、图表或屏幕设计。</li> <li><strong>提示词、任务和智能体指令：</strong> 添加可复用的提示词、交由 Codex 执行的操作，或给智能体的指导。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>插图：在页面中输入内容，依次添加标题、生成的引言、表格和图像。随后选中全部内容并一起删除，之后演示流程重新开始。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"work-with-selected-text\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">编辑选中的文字</h2> <p>选择页面中的文字会打开浮动工具栏。选择 <strong>Ask for change（提出修改）</strong>，即可描述要如何修改所选内容；也可以选择 <strong>Comment（评论）</strong>，针对这段内容展开讨论。</p> <p>你还可以将文字加粗、设为斜体或下划线、添加删除线、标记为行内代码，或添加链接。打开 <strong>Text（文本）</strong>，可以更改区块样式，例如标题、列表、清单或引用。</p>  <p><a id=\"rearrange-blocks\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">重新排列区块</h2> <p>随着页面内容逐渐成形，你可以移动区块。例如，将某项决定移到支持性研究上方，或把图像移到对应说明旁边。</p> <p>使用区块旁边的拖动手柄移动区块。选择手柄会打开该区块的选项。手柄也可移动列表或标题所在的整个章节；放下之前，请确认将要移动的是哪些内容。</p> <p><a id=\"draft-content-with-generate\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">使用“生成”起草内容</h2> <p>使用 <strong>Generate（生成）</strong> 可直接在页面中撰写初稿。打开 <code>/</code> 菜单，选择 <strong>Generate（生成）</strong>，并描述你希望添加的内容。说明用途、格式以及初稿必须保留的细节。例如：</p>  <p>请在页面中检查生成的文字。你可以接受、要求修改或撤销。需要生成新的页面内容时使用“生成”；需要为读者留下可复用的请求时，则使用“提示词”区块。</p> <p><a id=\"generate-images\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">生成图像</h2> <p>从 <code>/</code> 菜单中添加 <strong>Image（图像）</strong>区块，然后选择 <strong>Generate（生成）</strong>并描述你想要的图像。请说明主题、风格以及对页面重要的细节。例如：“为团队休整计划创作一幅黄昏时分的高山湖泊图像。”</p> <p>若要使用已有图像，请改选 <strong>Attach（附加）</strong>。有关更多图像创作和优化方式，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">图像生成</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"add-interactive-visualizations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">添加交互式可视化内容</h2> <p>可视化内容可以让读者在页面中探索生成的内容。你可以用图表说明流程、尝试屏幕设计，或创建一个可调整输入的小型计算器。请描述要展示的内容，以及读者应如何与它交互。</p> <p>输入 <code>/visualize</code>，再写下你的请求，然后选择匹配的菜单选项。例如：</p>  <p>菜单还提供了应用、屏幕设计、小组件或图表的起始模板。检查生成的内容，并在共享页面前试用其控件。要修改可视化内容，请在页面旁边的 ChatGPT 对话中说明要调整的内容和改动方式。</p> <p>更多示例、提示技巧，以及优化和共享可视化内容的指导，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-989576428b6123b7\">可视化</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"add-prompts-readers-can-run\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">添加读者可以运行的提示词</h2> <p><strong>提示词（Prompt）</strong>区块会保存一条请求，方便读者用它发起聊天。你可以从 <code>/</code> 菜单添加此区块，并在其中填写请求。例如，项目页面可以包含：</p> <blockquote> <p>总结此页面中尚待决定的问题，并建议接下来的三个步骤。</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以用提示词帮助读者开始探索内容、提出问题或安排后续工作。编辑时选择 <strong>Chat about this（就此内容聊天）</strong>即可运行提示词；阅读页面时，也可以直接选择该提示词。</p> <p><a id=\"mention-people-and-agents\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"mention-people-agents-files-and-chats\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">提及人员、智能体、文件和聊天</h2> <p>输入 <code>@</code> 并开始键入名称，即可提及某个人或你的某个智能体。提及人员可指定负责人或协作者；提及智能体可指明参与工作的智能体。在评论中，可以通过提及 <strong>ChatGPT</strong> 并说明具体请求来寻求帮助。有关与人员协作，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">在 Space 中协作</a>；有关请智能体起草、研究或修改内容，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-2d083870d670ea3a\">在 Space 中与智能体协作</a>。</p> <p>你也可以输入 <code>@</code>，查找并提及 Space 中的文件或 ChatGPT 聊天。提及文件可将计划与其参考材料关联起来；提及聊天可让读者查看某项决定背后的讨论。这样可以让来源始终与工作内容关联，而不必将来源内容复制到页面中。</p> <p><a id=\"organize-related-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">归纳相关工作</h2> <p>你可以创建子页面，将详细内容归纳在父页面下；也可以把同一主题或团队的相关页面放在一个空间中。如果只想引用另一个页面而不移动它，可以添加页面链接。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：光标将“发布清单”标题及其清单拖到“发布概览”标题和段落上方。每个章节的内容会一起移动。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"create-subpages\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">创建子页面</h3> <p>子页面是位于另一页面之内的页面。你可以用子页面简化项目概览，同时将研究、会议笔记或详细计划放在各自的子页面中。例如，发布计划页面可以包含客户研究和传播计划子页面。</p> <p>在父页面中输入 <code>/</code>，然后选择 <strong>Page（页面）</strong>即可创建子页面。为新页面起一个描述性标题，让读者知道其中包含什么内容。若要引用已经存在的页面，请改选 <strong>Link to page（链接到页面）</strong>。</p> <p>组织内容时请检查访问权限。页面可能会继承其共享 Space 或父页面的权限。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=understand-inherited-access\">理解继承的访问权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"revise-the-content\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_13\">修改内容</h2> <ol> <li>打开页面，并在旁边打开 ChatGPT。</li> <li>说明要修改的内容，并指出需要修改的文字。你可以要求新增章节、缩短初稿，或根据来源更新内容。</li> <li>阅读更新后的页面。你可以直接编辑，也可以要求 ChatGPT 再次修改。</li> </ol> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Rewrite the introduction for a reader who is new to this project. Preserve the scope, dates, decisions, and source links. Leave the rest of the page unchanged.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请为初次接触这个项目的读者重写引言。保留范围、日期、决定和来源链接。页面的其余部分保持不变。</div></div> <p><a id=\"give-wide-content-more-room\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_14\">为宽内容腾出更多空间</h2> <p>打开表格区块手柄菜单，并选择 <strong>Width（宽度）</strong>。选择 <strong>Normal（正常）</strong>、<strong>Flexible（灵活）</strong>或 <strong>Full width（全宽）</strong>，即可更改表格在页面中占用的宽度。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：光标打开 Space 表格的区块菜单，进入“宽度”，然后选择“全宽”。原本位于标准阅读栏中的表格随之扩展到页面边缘。</p> </blockquote> <p>表格的 <strong>Fit（适配）</strong>菜单提供多种列宽调整方式。在提供此选项时，选择 <strong>For readability（便于阅读）</strong>可为内容留出更多空间，或选择 <strong>Distribute columns evenly（均匀分布列宽）</strong>使列宽一致。请在实际使用页面的屏幕上检查显示效果。</p> <p><a id=\"review-changes-with-collaborators\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"comment-and-collaborate\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_15\">评论和协作</h2> <p>授予编辑权限后，协作者可以与你实时共同撰写。你可以使用评论针对某段内容提问或提供反馈，也可以在评论中提及 ChatGPT，请它协助处理该部分。</p> <p>在提供此选项时，选择 <strong>Show attribution（显示贡献者）</strong>即可查看内容由谁贡献。有关共享和访问控制，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">协作</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：突出显示的发布日期旁有一条评论串。Alex 请 Sam 确认日期；Sam 回复说该日期仍待批准。</p> </blockquote>","en":"<h1 id=\"work-with-pages\">Work with pages</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>A page is a document you can edit directly or with ChatGPT. Use it for notes, plans, research, or a shared reference you want to return to.</p> <p><a id=\"create-a-focused-page\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"create-a-page\">Create a page</h2> <p>Select <strong>New page</strong> in the Space sidebar, or ask ChatGPT to create a page from an existing conversation. Select <strong>Pages</strong> to find pages you've created or can access.</p> <p>Give the page a title, then type or paste your content. Add headings, lists, images, files, and tables as needed.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: The Space sidebar, with New page highlighted and navigation for All, Pages, Sites, Images, and Google Drive.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"add-content-with-the-insert-menu\">Add content with the insert menu</h2> <p>Pages organize content into blocks, such as headings, paragraphs, and tables. Type <code>/</code> while editing to open the insert menu and add a new block. Search for the content you want to add, then choose an option. Alongside headings, lists, and checklists, the menu offers ways to combine supporting material and interactive content:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Table, Code, and Highlight:</strong> Compare information, share code, or call attention to a note.</li> <li><strong>Image and File:</strong> Generate or upload images, or attach files readers can download.</li> <li><strong>Page and Link to page:</strong> Create a subpage or link to an existing page.</li> <li><strong>Files, Pages, and Chats:</strong> Reference existing material without copying it.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-989576428b6123b7\"><strong>Visualize</strong></a>: Create interactive calculators, diagrams, or screen designs.</li> <li><strong>Prompt, Task, and Agent Instructions:</strong> Add reusable prompts, actions for Codex, or guidance for agents.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Typing adds a heading, generated introduction, table, and image to one page. All content is selected and deleted together before the sequence restarts.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"work-with-selected-text\">Work with selected text</h2> <p>Select text on a page to open the floating toolbar. Use <strong>Ask for change</strong> to describe a revision to the selection, or <strong>Comment</strong> to start a discussion about that passage.</p> <p>You can also apply bold, italic, underline, or strikethrough formatting, mark inline code, and add a link. Open <strong>Text</strong> to change the block style, such as a heading, list, checklist, or quote.</p>  <h2 id=\"rearrange-blocks\">Rearrange blocks</h2> <p>Move blocks as your page takes shape. For example, bring a decision above its supporting research, or move an image next to the explanation it illustrates.</p> <p>Use the handle beside a block to drag it to a new position in the page. Select the handle to open the block's options. The handle can also move a list or a heading's section, so check which content you're moving before dropping it.</p> <h2 id=\"draft-content-with-generate\">Draft content with Generate</h2> <p>Use <strong>Generate</strong> to write a first draft directly in your page. Open the <code>/</code> menu, choose <strong>Generate</strong>, and describe what you want to add. Include the purpose, format, and details the draft should preserve. For example:</p>  <p>Review the generated text in place. You can accept it, ask for a change, or undo it. Use Generate when you want new page content; use a Prompt block when you want to leave a reusable request for readers.</p> <h2 id=\"generate-images\">Generate images</h2> <p>Add an <strong>Image</strong> block from the <code>/</code> menu, then choose <strong>Generate</strong> and describe the image you want. Include the subject, style, and details that matter for your page. For example: “Create a mountain lake at dusk for a team retreat plan.”</p> <p>To use an existing image, choose <strong>Attach</strong> instead. See <a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">Image generation</a> for more ways to create and refine images.</p> <h2 id=\"add-interactive-visualizations\">Add interactive visualizations</h2> <p>Visualizations let readers explore generated content inside the page. Use one to explain a process with a diagram, try a screen design, or let readers adjust inputs in a small calculator. Describe both what to show and how readers should interact with it.</p> <p>Type <code>/visualize</code> followed by your request, then choose the matching menu option. For example:</p>  <p>The menu also offers starting points for an app, screen design, widget, or diagram. Review the generated result and try its controls before sharing the page. To request a revision, describe the visualization and the change you want in ChatGPT alongside the page.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-989576428b6123b7\">Visualizations</a> for more examples, prompting tips, and guidance on refining and sharing a result.</p> <h2 id=\"add-prompts-readers-can-run\">Add prompts readers can run</h2> <p>A <strong>Prompt</strong> block stores a request that readers can use to start a chat. Add one from the <code>/</code> menu and write the request in the block. For example, a project page could include:</p> <blockquote> <p>Summarize the open decisions on this page and suggest the next three steps.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use prompts to give readers a starting point for exploring the work, asking questions, or planning a follow-up. Choose <strong>Chat about this</strong> to run the prompt while editing, or select the prompt when reading the page.</p> <p><a id=\"mention-people-and-agents\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"mention-people-agents-files-and-chats\">Mention people, agents, files, and chats</h2> <p>Type <code>@</code> and start a name to mention a person or one of your agents. Use a person mention to identify an owner or collaborator, and an agent mention to refer to the agent involved in the work. In a comment, mention <strong>ChatGPT</strong> with a specific request to ask it to help. See <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">Collaborate in Space</a> for working with people and <a href=\"#/article/a-2d083870d670ea3a\">Work with the agent in Space</a> for asking an agent to draft, research, or revise content.</p> <p>You can also type <code>@</code> to find and mention files in Space and your ChatGPT chats. Use a file mention to connect a plan to its supporting material, or a chat mention to point readers to a discussion behind a decision. These references keep the source close to the work without copying its contents into the page.</p> <h2 id=\"organize-related-work\">Organize related work</h2> <p>Create child pages to group details under a parent page, or keep related pages in a space for a topic or team. Link to another page when you want to reference it without moving it.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A cursor drags the Launch checklist heading and its checklist above the Launch overview heading and paragraph. Each section moves together.</p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"create-subpages\">Create subpages</h3> <p>A subpage is a page inside another page. Use subpages to keep a project overview short while giving research, meeting notes, or detailed plans their own space. For example, a launch page could contain subpages for customer research and a communications plan.</p> <p>In the parent page, type <code>/</code> and choose <strong>Page</strong> to create a subpage. Give the new page a descriptive title so readers can tell what belongs there. To refer to a page that already exists, choose <strong>Link to page</strong> instead.</p> <p>Review access as you organize the work. A page can inherit access from its shared Space or a parent page. See <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=understand-inherited-access\">Understand inherited access</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"revise-the-content\">Revise the content</h2> <ol> <li>Open the page and ChatGPT alongside it.</li> <li>Describe the change and identify the text to revise. You can ask for a new section, a shorter draft, or an update based on a source.</li> <li>Read the updated page. Edit it directly or ask for another change.</li> </ol> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Rewrite the introduction for a reader who is new to this project. Preserve the scope, dates, decisions, and source links. Leave the rest of the page unchanged.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"give-wide-content-more-room\">Give wide content more room</h2> <p>Open a table's block handle menu and select <strong>Width</strong>. Choose <strong>Normal</strong>, <strong>Flexible</strong>, or <strong>Full width</strong> to change how much of the page it uses.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A cursor opens a Space table's block menu, opens Width, and selects Full width. The same table expands from the normal reading column into the page margins.</p> </blockquote> <p>The table's <strong>Fit</strong> menu offers ways to size its columns. When offered, try <strong>For readability</strong> to give the content room or <strong>Distribute columns evenly</strong> for equally sized columns. Review the result on the screen where you'll use the page.</p> <p><a id=\"review-changes-with-collaborators\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"comment-and-collaborate\">Comment and collaborate</h2> <p>Share the page with edit access to write together in real time. Use comments for questions or feedback on a passage. You can also mention ChatGPT in a comment to ask for help with that part of the page.</p> <p>When available, select <strong>Show attribution</strong> to see who contributed. See <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b\">Collaboration</a> for sharing and access controls.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: A highlighted launch date has a comment thread. Alex asks Sam to confirm the date, and Sam replies that approval is still pending.</p> </blockquote>"};
